WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our first guest is the
co-founder of She Se Puede

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:04.137 align:start size:94% position:6%
a new digital
lifestyle community.

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:06.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's also
an Emmy Award-winning actor,

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:08.641
director, and producer who stars
in NBC's "Superstore,"

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:11.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
which premiers on October 29th
Let's take a look.

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:14.447
-Hey, any update on when you two
lovebirds are moving to Cali

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:17.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, um, with all of thi
craziness,

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
they've pushed my start date
so it's all a little

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:22.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
up in the air --
just like this virus.

00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:23.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just kidding.
It's not airborne.

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:26.059
Well, we don't know that.
It could be. Anyway --

00:00:26.059 --> 00:00:28.094 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, my God.
Hey, everyone's overreacting

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:30.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, no friggin' way
I'm missing out

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:31.498 line:92%
on spring break this year.

00:00:31.498 --> 00:00:33.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Actually, the latest articles
are saying

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:35.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
that washing your hands
isn't enough.

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:36.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
We should be wearing
face coverings,

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:39.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
avoiding large groups.
-Like, say, 50-plus employee

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:41.174 align:start size:94% position:6%
and an endless stream
of customers?

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:42.509 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-That sounds like here.

00:00:42.509 --> 00:00:44.377
-Please welcome back to the show
America Ferrera.

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:46.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's so nice to see you again.
How are you?

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:49.749 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hi, Seth. I'm doing well.
Thank you.

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:52.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And congratulations
are in order.

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:54.788 align:start size:94% position:6%
We've talked about the fac
that you have a son.

00:00:54.788 --> 00:00:57.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now since the last tim
you were here,

00:00:57.424 --> 00:00:59.292 line:92%
you have a daughter, correct

00:00:59.292 --> 00:01:01.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I do.
She was born in May,

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:04.798 align:start size:94% position:6%
kind of at the top of
quarantine.

00:01:04.798 --> 00:01:07.133 line:92%
And she's 5 months old now

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:10.770
-So I would imagine it's sort of
a pro and con situation.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:13.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
The con is, was it scary to,
you know,

00:01:13.773 --> 00:01:16.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
obviously have to go through
the medical care involved

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:18.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
with having a baby
during a pandemic?

00:01:18.545 --> 00:01:20.880 align:start size:94% position:6%
With the pro being,
you're home

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.082 line:92%
and you got to spend, obviously,

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:23.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
a lot of quality time,
I imagine.

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:26.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Yes.
I mean, having the baby

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:27.921 line:92%
is an isolating time anyway.

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:32.659
So it's nice to know I'm not
missing out on any fun anyway.

00:01:32.659 --> 00:01:35.728 size:84% position:42%
But it was a little bit
nerve-wracking, yes,

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:39.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the beginning to not be sur
what the situation

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:41.000 align:start size:94% position:6%
was going to be like
in hospitals.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know, things were
changing on a day-to-day basis

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:46.439 size:81% position:41%
So, I just had to kind
of breathe through it

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:47.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, you know,
hope for the best.

00:01:47.574 --> 00:01:50.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, you know, we --
we're all happy and health

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:54.147 size:78% position:39%
and that's all anyone
can ask for, so...

00:01:54.147 --> 00:01:56.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
we got lucky.
-Congratulations.

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:57.584 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I do have to ask how --

00:01:57.584 --> 00:02:00.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
I guess it's about a two-yea
difference with you kids?

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:03.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
How is your son reacting to hi
little sister so far?

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:05.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know what was great i
we were home with him

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:08.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
for so many weeks before
she came that I think

00:02:08.161 --> 00:02:11.931
he was actually relieved tha
out attention was not on him

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:13.833 line:92%
He was like, "Get another --

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:15.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, "Get another focus
Mom and Dad."

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:17.904 line:92%
So he's been actually grea

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:20.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
and has not taken anything
out on her,

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:23.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
which, I guess, is, you know
a good sign.

00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:25.044 line:92%
-That is a very good sign.

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:26.980 line:92%
I also want to congratulate yo

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:30.283 align:start size:94% position:6%
for this new platform
you launched.

00:02:30.283 --> 00:02:32.418 size:88% position:44% line:92%
This is basically for --

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:34.220 align:start size:94% position:6%
I guess, how would you
describe it?

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:34.988 size:78% position:39% line:92%
The Latina community?

00:02:34.988 --> 00:02:36.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that an accurate way
to describe it?

00:02:36.523 --> 00:02:40.860 size:81% position:41%
-Yeah, so She Se Puede
is a new online home,

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:45.465 size:84% position:42%
lifestyle and community
for Latinas by Latinas.

00:02:45.465 --> 00:02:50.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's meant to empower us t
live in our full power

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:53.940
and lead in our families and our
communities and in the country

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:59.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a mindset that Latinas ar
ready and poised to conque

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:01.381 line:92%
in every aspect of their life.

00:03:01.381 --> 00:03:05.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
In culture and in civic action
and politics, as well.

00:03:05.785 --> 00:03:07.320 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This both seems like
a good idea

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:09.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
and one that probably should
have happened already.

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:13.993
How did you come about being
in a position to launch it

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:18.665
-Well, there certainly have been
a number of -- of platform

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:21.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
existing to empower
and inspire Latinas.

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:25.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
She Se Puede came about --
Eva Longoria and myself

00:03:25.405 --> 00:03:29.742
and eight other incredible
women from -- from organizin

00:03:29.742 --> 00:03:33.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
and activism and from business
and from tech and research

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:36.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
came together to say,
what is missing for Latina

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:39.586 size:81% position:41%
in this conversation
about our empowerment?

00:03:39.586 --> 00:03:43.289 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because, you know, campaigns
and candidates

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:45.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
coming around two months
before an election

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:48.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
to knock on our door and say
"Your vote matters"

00:03:48.928 --> 00:03:49.662 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
is not cutting it.

00:03:49.662 --> 00:03:53.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's not going to lead to
the true empowerment of Latina

00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:56.336 align:start size:94% position:6%
using their power
and full force.

00:03:56.336 --> 00:03:59.239 line:92%
And what's missing is community.

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:01.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
And for us to not just hea
that our votes count,

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:05.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
but that our lives count,
that our joy and our struggles

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:10.049
and our goals, and that ever
aspect of our life matters

00:04:10.049 --> 00:04:14.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
And to celebrate the incredibl
contributions

00:04:14.554 --> 00:04:17.023 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we're making
across the board

00:04:17.023 --> 00:04:19.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
in every part of our
country.

00:04:19.192 --> 00:04:23.529 size:88% position:44%
You know, one quick fact
is that Latinos are 18%

00:04:23.529 --> 00:04:25.598 line:92%
of the population in the U.S.,

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:28.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
but we are 34%
of essentials workers.

00:04:28.668 --> 00:04:32.772
That in and of itself lets
you know that contribution

00:04:32.772 --> 00:04:35.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
that the Latino community is
making in this country

00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:39.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
that all too often are eithe
completely invisible

00:04:39.045 --> 00:04:42.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
in our culture,
and at worst are portrayed

00:04:42.949 --> 00:04:46.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
in really harmful ways
and with harmful stereotypes

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:48.488 line:92%
So we have new story to tell

00:04:48.488 --> 00:04:52.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is all about the badasse
that we currently are

00:04:52.425 --> 00:04:55.328
and the power that we hold
in our Latina community,

00:04:55.328 --> 00:04:59.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the difference we can make
when we are truly empowere

00:04:59.365 --> 00:05:01.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
and acting from
that empowerment.

00:05:01.401 --> 00:05:03.002 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is obviously something
you've been

00:05:03.002 --> 00:05:03.903 align:start size:94% position:6%
passionate about
for a long time.

00:05:03.903 --> 00:05:07.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
It must be exhilarating to hav
a place to put this energy

00:05:07.373 --> 00:05:11.411 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, yes, it's amazing,
and the response is amazing.

00:05:11.411 --> 00:05:12.645 line:92%
The fact that we launched this

00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:17.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
and very quickly had
tens of thousands of peopl

00:05:17.717 --> 00:05:20.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
in our community
hungry for this.

00:05:20.119 --> 00:05:21.554 line:92%
And especially in this year.

00:05:21.554 --> 00:05:25.024
Obviously we're 20 something
days away from an election

00:05:25.024 --> 00:05:28.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
where everything is at stake
and Latinas

00:05:28.995 --> 00:05:32.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
will be the deciders
in every state

00:05:32.031 --> 00:05:32.732 size:75% position:38% line:92%
across this country.

00:05:32.732 --> 00:05:36.235
In key states that matter fo
the outcome of this election

00:05:36.235 --> 00:05:39.205 size:88% position:44%
like Florida, Arizona,
Wisconsin, and Michigan,

00:05:39.205 --> 00:05:43.042 align:start size:94% position:6%
Latina voters can be decider
up and down the ballot.

00:05:43.042 --> 00:05:46.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so we all need to be
concerned with the empowerment

00:05:46.779 --> 00:05:49.382 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the resourcing of
Latino voters

00:05:49.382 --> 00:05:51.617 align:start size:94% position:6%
and specifically
Latina voters,

00:05:51.617 --> 00:05:55.054 align:start size:94% position:6%
who on their own make up
the margin of victory

00:05:55.054 --> 00:05:58.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
and defeat in so many states
across the country.

00:05:58.958 --> 00:06:02.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I also want to leave by askin
you about "Superstore."

00:06:02.662 --> 00:06:06.432
You are going to only do
two episodes this season.

00:06:06.432 --> 00:06:08.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's bittersweet.
It's the 100th episode

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:10.436 align:start size:94% position:6%
is your last one,
which really speaks to

00:06:10.436 --> 00:06:11.771 line:92%
the accomplishment of this show.

00:06:11.771 --> 00:06:14.707 size:88% position:44%
It's very hard to stay
on television that long.

00:06:14.707 --> 00:06:18.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
How do you feel about saying
goodbye to a family

00:06:18.144 --> 00:06:20.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you've been a part of
for so long?

00:06:20.313 --> 00:06:22.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, it's been a pretty long
goodbye.

00:06:22.515 --> 00:06:24.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was supposed to say goodby
back in March,

00:06:24.784 --> 00:06:28.121 align:start size:94% position:6%
but then we got shut down
for quarantine.

00:06:28.121 --> 00:06:30.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, you know, the joke is
that I've just, like,

00:06:30.456 --> 00:06:31.924 size:84% position:42% line:92%
said goodbye 500 times.

00:06:31.924 --> 00:06:33.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've had three
last table reads.

00:06:33.092 --> 00:06:35.661
Like, the cast couldn't be
more ready to just, like,

00:06:35.661 --> 00:06:36.729 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
get rid of me.

00:06:36.729 --> 00:06:38.331 line:92%
They've said goodbye already

00:06:38.331 --> 00:06:40.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I -- you know,
I love the show.

00:06:40.099 --> 00:06:42.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had such an amazing
five years.

00:06:42.902 --> 00:06:45.471 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got to work with this
incredible cast.

00:06:45.471 --> 00:06:47.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got to be
an executive producer.

00:06:47.607 --> 00:06:48.408 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I got to direct.

00:06:48.408 --> 00:06:50.209 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's been such an amazin
five years.

00:06:50.209 --> 00:06:53.312
The show -- I'm so proud o
the show, of what it is,

00:06:53.312 --> 00:06:55.982 size:84% position:42%
of how beloved it is by
its audience, and I --

00:06:55.982 --> 00:06:57.884 size:78% position:39%
You know, it's always
bittersweet to go,

00:06:57.884 --> 00:07:01.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I just couldn't be mor
proud of the five years

00:07:01.421 --> 00:07:03.189 line:92%
that I spent on "Superstore.

00:07:03.189 --> 00:07:05.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, congratulations
on that.

00:07:05.124 --> 00:07:07.026 align:start size:94% position:6%
Congratulations on
everything else.

00:07:07.026 --> 00:07:08.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's always such a delight
to see you.

00:07:08.594 --> 00:07:11.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you for being here.
-Thank you so much.

00:07:11.697 --> 00:07:13.666 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Please visit
shesepuede.org

00:07:13.666 --> 00:07:15.134 size:75% position:38%
for more information
on the organization.

00:07:15.134 --> 00:07:19.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
And "Superstore" premieres
October 29th right here on NBC

